.TH D3HOME 1 "2026-08-20" "d3home 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
d3home \- control smart home devices over the local network
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B d3home
.RI < device-or-alias >
.RI < action >
.RI [ args ...]
.br
.B d3home
.RI < builtin >
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B d3home
speaks to smart home devices directly on the local network, without a cloud
account and without the vendor's application. The first word of a command is
a device name, or any alias given to it in the configuration, so
.B d3home k start 80
works once
.B k
is an alias.
.PP
Devices are found over mDNS and addressed over UDP. Nothing leaves the local
network.
.SH KETTLE ACTIONS
.TP
.B status
Show mode, current and target temperature, and the error flag.
.TP
.B start ", " on
Heat to 100 degrees Celsius.
.TP
.BI start " temp"
Heat to
.I temp
degrees Celsius.
.TP
.BI set " temp"
Set the target without starting, or retarget a heat already running.
.TP
.B off ", " stop
Stop heating.
.TP
.B watch
Stream events until
.B q
or Ctrl-C. Reconnects by itself when the kettle is put back on its base.
.TP
.B trace
Every report the device makes, with protocol codes. For taking the protocol
apart rather than for daily use.
.SH BUILTIN COMMANDS
.TP
.BI add " [link]"
Register a device: paste the share link from the vendor application, answer
the prompts, or pass
.BR \-\-name ", " \-\-mac ", " \-\-token ", " \-\-model " and " \-\-vendor .
.TP
.B daemon
Watch the configured devices and send a notification when something happens.
Runs in the foreground and does not fork; see
.B FILES
for the supervisor units.
.TP
.B discover
Find devices on the local network.
.TP
.B devices
List what is configured.
.TP
.BI "alias add" " alias device"
Give
.I device
the alias
.IR alias .
.TP
.BI "alias rm" " alias"
Remove
.IR alias .
.TP
.BI completions " shell"
Print a completion script for bash, zsh or fish.
.TP
.B help
Print the built-in help.
.SH OPTIONS
Options are accepted anywhere on the command line: before the device word,
after the action, or after the action's own arguments.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output. Errors honour it too.
.TP
.BI \-\-device " name"
Act on
.IR name ,
instead of taking the device from the first word.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " path"
Use
.I path
as the device registry.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the built-in help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Internal error: a bug, or a filesystem failure.
.TP
.B 2
Usage or configuration error.
.TP
.B 3
The device was not found on the network.
.TP
.B 4
The device rejected the token.
.TP
.B 5
The device did not answer in time.
.TP
.B 6
The device reported an error of its own.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/d3home/devices.toml
The device registry, holding one entry per device with its token. Created by
.B d3home add
with owner-only permissions.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/d3home/contrib/
Example supervisor units: a systemd user unit, a macOS LaunchAgent and a
Windows scheduled task, all of which run the daemon in the logged-in user's
session.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Set to any value to suppress colour. Colour is also suppressed automatically
when the output is not a terminal.
.SH NOTES
The device holds a single token, which is also what the vendor's application
uses. Registering d3home does not revoke it, and the application keeps
working.
.SH SEE ALSO
The protocol is documented in
.I /usr/share/doc/d3home/protocol.md
and at
.UR https://github.com/Demetri0/d3-home
.UE .
